  "lineage": "Banjar oral poetry of South Kalimantan in which one or two performers (pamadihinan) improvise rhymed quatrains, humorous, advisory or topical, while beating a terbang frame drum themselves (the generic frame-drum card stands in); when two perform they answer and tease each other in turn. It is performed at weddings and celebrations and circulates widely on cassette and VCD.",
